## From Pattern to Machine Code

### Match Compilation

```xiom
// XIOM:
match value {
  0 => "zero",
  1 => "one",
  2 => "two",
  _ => "many",
}

// Compiled to: JUMP TABLE (O(1))
// jump_table[value] -> target address
//   [0]: load "zero"
//   [1]: load "one"
//   [2]: load "two"
//   [3+]: load "many"
```

vs sparse values:

```xiom
match value {
  0 => "zero",
  1000 => "thousand",
  _ => "other",
}

// Compiled to: if-else chain
// if value == 0 { "zero" }
// else if value == 1000 { "thousand" }
// else { "other" }
```

### Enum Layout

```xiom
pub enum Option[Int] {
  Some(Int),
  None,
}

// Memory layout:
// Some(42):  [tag: 0] [payload: 42]
// None:      [tag: 1] [payload: 0 (unused)]
```

Niche optimization:

```xiom
pub enum Option[Bool] {
  Some(Bool),
  None,
}

// Optimized layout (1 byte!):
// Some(false): 0x00
// Some(true):  0x01
// None:        0x02  (Bool only uses 0 and 1, so 2 represents None)
```

### Closure Compilation

```xiom
// XIOM:
let factor = 10;
let multiply = |x| x * factor;

// Compiled to STRUCT + CALL:
pub type Closure_1 = {
  factor: Int,  // Captured variable
}

impl Fn(Int) -> Int for Closure_1 {
  fn call(self: &Closure_1, x: Int) -> Int {
    return x * self.factor;
  }
}

let multiply = Closure_1{ factor: 10 };
let result = multiply.call(5);
```

### Generic Monomorphization

```xiom
// Generic code:
fn identity[T](x: T) -> T { return x; }

// After monomorphization (compile-time):
fn identity_Int(x: Int) -> Int { return x; }
fn identity_Str(x: Str) -> Str { return x; }
fn identity_Bool(x: Bool) -> Bool { return x; }
// No generic code at runtime — fully specialized!
```

### Iterator Compilation

```xiom
let sum = nums.iter().filter(|n| n > 0).map(|n| n * 2).sum();

// Compiled to SINGLE LOOP (no intermediate allocations):
var sum = 0;
var i = 0;
while i < nums.len() {
  let n = nums[i];
  if n > 0 {
    sum = sum + n * 2;
  }
  i = i + 1;
}
```

syntax_ref:
// Match on dense small ints → jump table (fast)
// Match on sparse values → if-else chain
// Iterators → fused single loops
// Generics → monomorphized concrete functions

